\line }{\loch\lang1025\loch
Fu}{\loch\lang1025\loch
{\*\bkmkend __DdeLink__5_256217038}nction Smarpod_FindReference does not move SmarPods with distance-coded reference-marks to the zero position anymore. This avoids unneccesary movements when referencing. Please check that the correct behavior of your programs does not depend on the zero pose after referencing! }
\par \pard\plain \s47\rtlch\af20\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1081\hich\af7\loch\sl288\slmult1\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\faauto\fi-210\li345\lin345\sb0\sa51\ltrpar\cf1\f7\fs16\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af15\langfe1081\sl288\slmult1\fi-210\li345\lin345\ri0\rin0{\loch\lang1025\loch
IMPORTANT: BEHAVIOR MODIFICATION}{\loch
\line }{\loch\lang1025\loch
Function Smarpod_ReleaseAll does not implicitly stop the positioners. If the positioners are in holding mode they will stay in that mode after ReleaseAll. If the SmarPod should not keep the holding mode after the program has quit, call Smarpod_Stop explicitly before ReleaseAll. }
